.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt NSHD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nshd
.Nd network configuration daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl dv
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads the system's configuration for
.Xr nsh 8 ,
which asks it over a socket.
It is privilege separated.
The parent process, as root, binds the sockets and starts six children:
.Bl -tag -width "frontend"
.It relay
Runs as _nshd in a
.Xr chroot 2 ,
and passes on what one child may send another, and nothing else.
.It show
Runs as _nshd in a
.Xr chroot 2
and answers the read-only socket, with what anyone may see.
It has no path to the others.
.It frontend
Runs as _nshd in a
.Xr chroot 2
and answers the read-write socket.
Each client is a session, which asks one thing at a time.
.It config
Runs as _nshd in a
.Xr chroot 2 ,
holds the sessions, and asks kernel for what they need.
.It kernel
Runs as root, and reads the configuration from the kernel.
It answers config and no one else.
.It archive
Runs as _nshd in a
.Xr chroot 2 ,
with kernel its one peer.
It keeps nothing yet.
.El
.Pp
Each child but relay has one pipe, to relay.
The parent reads only what relay tells it.
A child that exits, or sends what it may not, is started again, and
those that talk to it forget what it held: its sessions, or the answers
it had not yet given.
A child that fails five times in a minute stays down.
Then the others answer for it, or, for show and frontend, its socket
refuses connections.
If relay fails, every child starts again with it; if relay fails five
times in a minute,
.Nm
exits.
.Pp
Only root and the members of the group _nshd may connect to the
read-write socket, and every session there may see the running
configuration.
The read-only socket is for anyone.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d
Do not daemonize, and log to standard error.
.It Fl v
Produce more verbose output.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/run/nshd.ro.sockXX" -compact
.It Pa /var/run/nshd.sock
the read-write socket, mode 0660, group _nshd
.It Pa /var/run/nshd.ro.sock
the read-only socket, mode 0666
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nsh 8
